mode: "100644"
text: "# X (Twitter) 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly. Figures vary across sources; the open-source weights are the anchor.*\n\n## The engine: conversation, not broadcasting\nX open-sourced its ranking (re-released by xAI Jan 2026; pledged 4-week updates). The weights are\nblunt — **a reply is worth ~27× a like, and an author-reply chain ~150× a like.** Widely-cited\nrelative weights: Retweet ×20 · Reply ×13.5 · Profile click ×12 · Link click ×11 · Bookmark ×10 ·\nLike ×1. **Likes barely count; conversation dominates.** Bookmarks signal lasting value.\n\n## First-hour velocity + reach mechanics\n- **Engagement velocity in the first 30–60 min** is the strongest signal for **out-of-network / For\n  You** reach (where discovery happens). Post when your audience is online; engage your own replies fast.\n- **TweepCred** (0–100, PageRank-style): below ~**65**, only ~3 of your posts are considered for\n  distribution; above it, all are eligible. **Premium adds +4 to +16.** **SimClusters** = topic\n  clusters; reach comes from engagement by users in the target's cluster.\n- Dwell time + 70+ behavioral signals (hover, opening replies, returning to a post).\n\n## Premium is now a baseline (state it honestly)\nPremium gives a **significant reach multiplier** (sources range ~2.4× to ~4–8×, some say ~10×;\nverify-quarterly) and **free accounts see near-zero median reach.** It also unlocks **25,000-char\nlong-form**, **higher-ranked replies**, **edit**, **analytics**, revenue share, Grok. **Caveat:** it\n**amplifies** quality, it doesn't replace it — Premium + mediocre content still loses.\n\n## Format hierarchy (2026 shifts)\n- **Long-form single posts** (Premium, up to 25k chars) are now often favored **over multi-tweet\n  threads** for distribution. Threads still build authority when there's a real arc.\n- **Native video** is heavily pushed (~42% of media posts); **images ~2× text engagement**;\n  **Articles are now boosted** (a reversal — X wants to be \"where you discover everything\").\n- **External links are suppressed** — ~30–50% less reach in the main post (near-zero non-Premium).\n  **Put the link in the first reply.** Polls = high engagement, weaker follower conversion.\n- **Hashtags:** 1–2 (≈ +21% lift); **3+ penalized** (≈ −17%); zero is fine.\n\n## Replies = the afterburner\nA standout reply on a bigger account's post surfaces in **For You** to people who engaged with the\noriginal (often **5–20× your baseline**). Use a split weighted to **larger niche accounts** (~60/30/10)\nto enter high-traffic conversations and the right cluster. **Quote posts:** always add original\ncommentary; **copy-paste/duplicate triggers a spam filter** and kills reach.\n\n## Cadence + anti-patterns\n**2–3 quality posts/day** (3–5 under 5k followers incl. replies), **spaced 30–60 min**; volume with low\nper-post engagement is penalized. **Penalized:** engagement-bait (\"RT if…\"), pods/purchased/coordinated\namplification, copy-paste virality, low-value \"good morning\". **Accuracy has a distribution\nconsequence** — an active **Community Note** correction reduces reach.\n\n## Monetization + fit (honest)\nCreator revenue-share is real but **X publishes no payout totals**; the pool keys on **verified/Premium-user\nengagement, not followers** (eligibility now from ~500 followers), and earnings are **extremely\nconcentrated** — most monetized creators make a few dollars to a few hundred per quarter\n(verify-quarterly). Don't promise income.\n**Topic amplification zones:** AI/tech, politics/current events, finance/crypto, sports — \"expertise\nmoment\" posts (a fast, informed take on breaking niche news) are the highest-ROI action. **Honest fit:**\nX has the **lowest engagement rate** of the majors; it's strong for **B2B, tech, finance, thought\nleadership, real-time/news, customer service** — not a default for consumer brands targeting under-25s.\nNew: **Communities** public (Feb 2026), **Grok** deeply integrated, **X Chat** encrypted DMs.\n"
